Subject: [PATCH 06872/11362] [outer-loop] ARC sp80 round-5: L5->L6, FULL GAME
 CLEAR

Round-5 claude-fable-5 attempt on sp80 solved L6, the final level of the
six-level game. Resolves round-4's "at least one final routing or hidden
condition is still unresolved" with a precise geometric diagnosis: round
4's layout already colored all four sockets, but the right branch struck
the solid top of the right socket at y=29..31 even though the socket
glyph visibly changed color -- a glyph-color change does not mean the
stream actually entered through the open side. Moving the right-turn
elbow down exactly one 3-pixel cell shifts the outflow through the
socket's actual open side and wins live.

Compressed to a 37-action suffix after the 278-action prefix (315 total);
fresh-reset reproduce() passed with reached_level=6. Independently
re-verified by the outer loop: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via a new
resolver priority branch, all 5 confirmed level=6, state=GameState.WIN --
the game's full 6 levels are now cleared.

reproducible_total_levels 152 -> 153 (14th full game clear).
arc_count_integrity_lint.py exit 0.

